From 66ba76208e180bc38085593fc809988bcba675c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:56:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] fix(backend): run camera publishers from Studio and
 recover dead ones

Changing a camera's resolution in the camera form asked the running
publisher to reconfigure itself in place, which races its capture loop and
killed it. Its service then outlived it (subscribers in the backend kept it
open), so SharedCamera.connect found it "served", never started a publisher,
and every later connect timed out until Studio was restarted.

Studio now starts its publishers itself (utils.camera_publishers), one per
camera device, with exactly the requested settings: other settings stop the
running publisher and wait for it to release the camera before the new one
starts (or are refused when the camera must keep its settings), a dead
publisher is replaced, one that delivers nothing is restarted, and recording
validates the publisher's settings instead of silently using others.
Publishers are recorded on disk and stopped on shutdown; at startup,
publishers a killed backend left behind are stopped.

SIGTERM looked ignored because uvicorn waits forever for open connections'
tasks: a camera preview whose camera sent nothing never noticed its socket
closing. Previews now watch their socket and report a stalled camera, the
server has a graceful-shutdown timeout, and camera errors such as an
unavailable RealSense mode reach the preview as a message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
